{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty","id":1403170,"title":"So I have no idea how to judge encounter difficulty...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-16T19:24:51-07:00","id":1403170,"title":"So I have no idea how to judge encounter difficulty...","content":"...so I've mostly been trying to go with what makes sense in-world, which has been working well so far. But as of last session, the local authorities are fully aware that the players are Solars <i>and </i>acting against them, and have logically decided that the best option is to hit them with overwhelming force. And now I feel like I kind of need an idea about how rough the fight is going to be, should it happen. So, uh... what kind of odds am I looking at here? Will the battle wind up being easy, risky, or overpowering? <br /> <br /> The players are all well spec'd for fighting-- they've all got good Dex and combat skills. All three are Essence 1 with 25 experience points. Most of their local support is in spy networks and public opinion, but they recently co-opted a sorcerer and the eight Agata she'd summoned.<ul><li>The Eclipse has a Throwing Charm or two, Blinding Battle Feint, and enough stealth to do pull off combat stealth.</li> <li>The Zenith has something like a half dozen Melee Charms-- I remember Excellent Strike, Fire and Stones, One Weapon/Two Blows, Glorious Solar Saber, and Dipping Swallow. She's been wrecking a lot of face in encounters so far.</li> <li>The Dawn took a blend of White Reaper and Righteous Devil Dawn-- he's partway down both trees, and has an artifact weapon that functions as both spear and firewand (with a reflexive-loading Evocation).</li> </ul><br /> The opposition has limited resources, what with being on an island, and the players have been picking away at them for a while--just last session they smashed the last of their mortal soldiers. But there's plenty of supernatural power...<ul><li>Two Dragonblooded, one Essence 3 Air aspect and one Essence 2.Earth aspect.<ul><li>The Air aspect has the Breath Seizing Technique, Wrathful Winds, and Wind Dragon's Speed Charms from the core book. He's also got custom charms to extend his melee attacks as far as medium range, and to make a withering attack against all within close range (without gaining any of the initiative). He's got an artifact chain shirt.</li> <li>The Earth aspect has Shattering Strike and Earthshaker Attack from the core book. He's also immune to being shoved around and has a huge +8 Soak/Hardness vs one attack charm.</li> </ul></li> <li>A size 1 battle group of Immaculate Monks</li> <li>A size 1 battle group of golems</li> </ul><br /> Many thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T20:33:05-07:00","id":1403175,"title":"","content":"What are each characters' Join battle, main attack pool, parry and dodge DV, and soak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T22:44:45-07:00","id":1403179,"title":"","content":"If this is just one fight and that's all the opposition can muster it's going to be mega easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T23:50:13-07:00","id":1403189,"title":"","content":"Dawn.<br /> <br /> The PCs are asleep in their beds.<br /> <br /> The Earth Aspect and Golems are beneath them, sappers. They collapse the building. Roll (Perception+Athletics-3*) -- five successes means they notice what's going on and brace against the collapse taking no damage, three successes and they take a Short range fall and are left Prone, fewer than three successes and they take the full Medium range fall and are Prone. Regardless, the characters are left in a pit under their residency. This kills the sorceress and frees the agata, or at least incapacitates her and the agata fly her to safety abandoning the PCs.<br /> <br /> The pit is lined with pitch, which the Earth Aspect ignites. The Earth Aspect Withdraws through the sapping tunnels, collapsing them behind him. The PCs fight the golems (who have been rendered fireproof, and have Elite drill and Might 2) in the midst of a ranging bonfire hazard. The Air Aspect uses Voice on the Wind to deliver Command actions to the Battlegroup from a safe distance.<br /> <br /> The golems explode on death. The explosion knocks anyone in Close range Prone and releases cursed golem dust. Anyone in Short range must roll to resist poison equivalent to Curare as they risk inhaling the dust.<br /> <br /> Once the golems are defeated, it's only a Difficulty 2 roll to climb out of the pit. Impress upon the PCs that they <i>really</i> want to pass that roll. If the PCs fail/refuse, point out that they're below sea level on an island and at any moment the Dragon-Blooded could flood them out with seawater and drown them like dogs.<br /> <br /> Both Dragon-Blooded and the monks are waiting for them. The Earth Aspect will use Smashing attacks to try to knock the PCs back into the pit (Short range fall). The Abbott of the monks will use Command actions on the Battlegroup. The Air Aspect does their thing.<br /> <br /> If things really go south for the players, the Agata can rescue them -- but being unpredictable, flighty beings, this can't be relied on. If you need the sorceress to live, then don't have her and the demons bunk with the PCs.<br /> <br /> *No, the players may not substitute for (Wits+Dodge)<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> That ought to give you a &quot;risky&quot; encounter without over much playing unfair.<br /> <br /> For an overwhelming encounter, have the sorceress betray them, and attack from the back of an Agata in mid-air in the final battle, no roll to avoid the fall without Charms, replace the burning pitch with lava, have the golems Ambush the PCs in the pit, climbing out of the pit now means closing Medium to Short to Close through Difficult Terrain, have the Immaculates pepper the PCs with poison arrows as they climb out the pit, and give the Air Aspect Yozi Venom and start them in Stealth.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to post the character sheets, I'm happy to advise further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-17-2020, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T03:38:13-07:00","id":1403203,"title":"","content":"What's that sorceress worth to them?<br /> My experience when it comes to encounter planning is that an ally in mortal danger is almost always way more valuable than one killed outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T08:27:13-07:00","id":1403235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403189#post1403189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dawn.<br /> <br /> Snip<br /> <br /> If you wanted to post the character sheets, I'm happy to advise further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T10:00:42-07:00","id":1403245,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2783_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2783\" data-vbnamecard=\"2783\">Tytalus</a>: I don't have their sheets, but they're all standing around 4/4 or 5/5 in their main combat skills, but have crappy soak by reason of being mostly unarmored.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>: They're not particularly attached to her-- about two sessions ago they tore through her guards and she went &quot;I surrender, I never liked those guys anyway!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403189#post1403189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That ought to give you a &quot;risky&quot; encounter without over much playing unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is amazingly brutal and I am Here For It. More importantly, it gives me a much better idea of how far I can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T11:44:35-07:00","id":1403260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403203#post1403203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's that sorceress worth to them?<br /> My experience when it comes to encounter planning is that an ally in mortal danger is almost always way more valuable than one killed outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree. But 8 agata is soooo hard to counter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403235#post1403235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stand corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely used your encounter design philosophy, sifu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403245#post1403245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is amazingly brutal and I am Here For It. More importantly, it gives me a much better idea of how far I can go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, this should be a landmark battle. Pulling a stunt like this regularly is just going to cause an arms race. Your PCs should generally feel awesome and invested enough in combat, they shouldn't feel a heartbeat away from death at all times. But they should also not be casual about revealing themselves as Anathema or fighting the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-17-2020, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T14:05:14-07:00","id":1403284,"title":"","content":"They have a spy network on their side and their enemies manage a weeks (at least, medium range is a big hole) work of sapping literally right under them without anyone noticing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-17-2020, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T14:08:08-07:00","id":1403285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403284#post1403284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a spy network on their side an their enemies manage a weeks work of sapping literally right under them without anyone noticing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their enemies who are a literal demi-god of earth and their force of mystic golems?<br /> <br /> I reckon they can carry out a couple months worth of sapping in an hour or two.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Dragon-Blooded are in power here. On an island. It's conceivable that a tunnel network already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T14:18:48-07:00","id":1403289,"title":"","content":"I was counting on considerable magic to make it a week, medium range is like 50m-ish, that's a gigantic pit that the players happen to be sleeping over. Fall damage is also pretty brutal, if someone fails to get 3 successes and doesn't have Soaring Crane Leap or an Ox-Body they are most likely incapacitated.<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear i think it sounds like a great fight with the exceptioin of the fall damage at the start which is a bit 'succeed or you don't get to play' combined with an improbable set-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-17-2020, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T17:01:46-07:00","id":1403303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403260#post1403260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just to be clear, this should be a landmark battle. Pulling a stunt like this regularly is just going to cause an arms race. Your PCs should generally feel awesome and invested enough in combat, they shouldn't feel a heartbeat away from death at all times. But they should also not be casual about revealing themselves as Anathema or fighting the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. This would be the climax of the first stage of the campaign, leaving the players in charge of a good-sized island.<br /> <br /> As for the spy network thing, I've got some mechanics in place (based on Sandact6's Creation Overlords) to make the spy-vs-spy &quot;fair.&quot; Finding the PCs and setting up an ambush on that scale would be damn hard, but the players are pretty white knight-y. Luring them to a prepared site by threatening to kill a bunch of innocents will be a lot easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T18:09:37-07:00","id":1403315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403289#post1403289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was counting on considerable magic to make it a week, medium range is like 50m-ish, that's a gigantic pit that the players happen to be sleeping</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragonblooded charm Ramparts of Obedient Earth lets you create a sinkhole under the feet of a thousand man Battlegroup, in a big enough radius to extend past their lines out to Short range, and do so fast enough that they can\u2019t maneuver out of it, and that\u2019s one of its two least impressive settings. The other being to wrench earthen fortifications from the ground and raise them up as the enemy is charging them. The point is it\u2019s not even outside the scope of Dragonblooded charms to instantly create a very large sinkhole on their own. The fact that it takes several hours and a small army of golems speaks to it not being very powerful terrestrial magic.<br /> <br /> Medium range fall might be a bit intense, but it depends a bit on the PCs. If everyone has even decent perception/athletics/awareness with excellencies the risk is very small that anyone is going to straight up fail and take full fall damage. At least it is if you properly impress on them what\u2019s at stake and they stunt and spend Essence. Characters with the worst odds may also wish to spend a willpower, which would make the difficulty 3 roll almost an automatic success.<br /> <br /> We still tease our one friend about the time he half-excellencied his resolve against the Nephrack\u2019s shattered mirror charm and ended up plugging the Dawn in the back of the head with an arrow. Four more motes man, that was the difference between winning and losing that battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T19:25:01-07:00","id":1403321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403315#post1403315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragonblooded charm Ramparts of Obedient Earth lets you create a sinkhole under the feet of a thousand man Battlegroup, in a big enough radius to extend past their lines out to Short range, and do so fast enough that they can\u2019t maneuver out of it, and that\u2019s one of its two least impressive settings. The other being to wrench earthen fortifications from the ground and raise them up as the enemy is charging them. </div> </div> </div> </div>The Rampharts sinkhole creates difficult terrain, not a death-pit. Reshape Battlefield resculpts the battlefield &quot;before that battle&quot; and there is no enemy battle group for the Earth Aspect to target with either effect so that's no help here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403315#post1403315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Medium range fall might be a bit intense, but it depends a bit on the PCs. If everyone has even decent perception/athletics/awareness with excellencies the risk is very small that anyone is going to straight up fail and take full fall damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per+Athletics <b>-3</b>. If anyone's sitting at average Per and no Athletics excellency even with a stunt and a WP they are not unlikely to eat the full 4 auto lethal and 7 dice bashing, after which they probably eat the bonfire due to wound penalties and then are out in short order.<br /> <br /> Being incapacitated in your sleep and then getting to watch the other players fight the big climatic battle without you sounds like a bummer, so I would personally try to avoid it as a possibility. If everyone's rocking Athetics(F) 5 it's another story.<br /> <br /> Also while I get wanting to cut down on rolling for noticing the hazard and then a second roll to avoid the damage, having Awarness play no part in noticing the hazard feels a bit arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T20:40:04-07:00","id":1403329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403321#post1403321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rampharts sinkhole creates difficult terrain, not a death-pit. Reshape Battlefield resculpts the battlefield &quot;before that battle&quot; and there is no enemy battle group for the Earth Aspect to target with either effect so that's no help here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Ramparts of Obedient Earth specifically is not going to help here, but for a type of exalt that can pull feats like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w_Ko7VusR04\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, it's not beyond the scope of power that they could undermine a house in even a few minutes. For those Exalted by the Earth Dragon, manipulating the earth is one of their things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403321#post1403321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also while I get wanting to cut down on rolling for noticing the hazard and then a second roll to avoid the damage, having Awarness play no part in noticing the hazard feels a bit arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that could maybe be separated into two rolls. If it's just everyone rolling and then effect those can tend to go fast. Maybe one percep+aware roll at difficulty 3 with a -3 penalty for sleeping, then afterwards a difficulty 3 roll to slow the fall, 5 to negate it entirely, but if you're still asleep you take the -3 penalty here too. It maybe should even be a -5 penalty at that point, having the ground drop out from under you while you're prone and unconscious is pretty intense, but we can say the building doesn't fully go into freefall right away or something like that.<br /> <br /> Again though, it depends on your group. If everyone took Awareness 5 because, <i>DUH</i>, and everyone took at least Athletics 3 and an excellency, then that's an easily beaten pair of challenges. Although they would be costly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T22:11:20-07:00","id":1403339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403321#post1403321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per+Athletics <b>-3</b>. If anyone's sitting at average Per and no Athletics excellency even with a stunt and a WP they are not unlikely to eat the full 4 auto lethal and 7 dice bashing, after which they probably eat the bonfire due to wound penalties and then are out in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is pretty noticeable, though, that you are trying to call this trick too heavy handed on the basis of &quot;it kills a normal, not particularly athletic person&quot;.<br /> <br /> And well, yeah. An exalt with Per 2, a stunt and a wp has a chance of basically halving that damage with literally nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T01:14:28-07:00","id":1403351,"title":"","content":"A good general rule I tend to use is to face the players with combat encounters at least as powerful as them, and then do two things:<br /> <br /> 1) grapple. In my experience, nothing scares the players as much as being grappled and then having other minions come over and try to kill deliver killing blows. This also gives great opertunities for the other players to rescue them, which can make for some interesting player and character dynamics with the whole &quot;I saved you&quot; VS &quot;I totally had that under control&quot; fun stuff<br /> <br /> 2) you don't have to kill them outright... I don't recall the exact wording of the rules, but maiming blows are still a thing in 3rd, right? Instead of delivering a killing blow, chop off an arm or a leg. Or perhaps simply have the opponent disarm the player and demand their surrender. Similarly to the first point, basically put them in a position where the others have to save them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And ya, ambushes with put traps that forcibly separate them if they dont have athlethtics or fast crafting charms to dig their way out, those work great for this. If the players rely too much on magical or demonic transportation, have a sorcerer lie in ambush and counterspell or banish their transport out from under them. that's a great way to initiate a battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T01:25:59-07:00","id":1403353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403339#post1403339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is pretty noticeable, though, that you are trying to call this trick too heavy handed on the basis of &quot;it kills a normal, not particularly athletic person&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kills a pretty athletic person with bad luck. You can be a pretty athletic without being superhumanly (excellency) athletic.<br /> <br /> I'm calling it heavy handed based on that the encounter mostly boils down to if everyone has the Athletics excellency or not, which yes most exalted tend to end up having but it's crazy punishing if you don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403339#post1403339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An exalt with Per 2, a stunt and a wp has a chance of basically halving that damage with literally nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 1 in 10 chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T02:02:52-07:00","id":1403357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403321#post1403321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rampharts sinkhole creates difficult terrain, not a death-pit. Reshape Battlefield resculpts the battlefield &quot;before that battle&quot; and there is no enemy battle group for the Earth Aspect to target with either effect so that's no help here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Per+Athletics <b>-3</b>. If anyone's sitting at average Per and no Athletics excellency even with a stunt and a WP they are not unlikely to eat the full 4 auto lethal and 7 dice bashing, after which they probably eat the bonfire due to wound penalties and then are out in short order.<br /> <br /> Being incapacitated in your sleep and then getting to watch the other players fight the big climatic battle without you sounds like a bummer, so I would personally try to avoid it as a possibility. If everyone's rocking Athetics(F) 5 it's another story.<br /> <br /> Also while I get wanting to cut down on rolling for noticing the hazard and then a second roll to avoid the damage, having Awarness play no part in noticing the hazard feels a bit arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The players are all well spec'd for fighting&quot;<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't a proscriptive RPG. Though Vance has clarified this is not the intent, I'd allow the use of Reflexive Charms which make sense. If you've got, say, the Dodge Charm Reflex Sidestep Technique (which lets you dodge attacks and traps you didn't see coming), it would be not unreasonable to cancel the penalty for being asleep -- even though it's not a Dodge roll and Evasion doesn't apply. Or allow the Awareness Charm Surprise Anticipation Method (which helps stop you being taken by surprise) to apply to the roll. Or let a Resistance Supernal Stunt how she toughs out the fall with Adament Skin Technique (which can stop uncountable damage from scenery effects). Or if someone is awake -- either keeping watch, or rising before sunrise -- they don't take the -3, and could even wake the others perhaps.<br /> <br /> Willpower and a level 2 Stunt gives you two successes and reduces the penalty to -1. (That's a 40% chance of success with Perception 2 and literally nothing else.) A noticeably athletic person of average perception (3+2) gets at least 3 successes 87% of the time.<br /> <br /> If that's still too difficult for your party then lower the difficulty. Or let them have it as Wits+Dodge or Dexterity+Awareness or some other &quot;guarenteed 11&quot; pool. Rule that their beds break the fall, reducing the guaranteed damage to Bashing and eliminate the rolled damage. This is just an idea, scale it to suit.<br /> <br /> The point of the fall is to soften them up. Either by getting them to spend precious motes and willpower or by giving them wound penalties. That's how the Wyld Hunt operates. Because the PCs are going to be basically unstoppable in any fair fight.<br /> <br /> Also Crippling injuries are a thing. Take one instead of being put out of the final fight.<br /> <br /> If the bonfire hazard is a problem, have the pitch burn out, or encourage the PCs to put the fire out with a Gambit. Or make the pit have patches of bonfire, but reduce the overall hazard to sandstorm levels.<br /> <br /> This is just one idea on how to challenge 3 combat invested Solars with two Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The list of Charms given in a splat book is not the sum total of all known magic the splat is capable of. The Dragon-Blooded can move earth around. Digging a fifty foot pit doesn't strike me as beyond the Princes of the Earth, whether there's an opposing battlegroup or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403353#post1403353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm calling it heavy handed based on that the encounter mostly boils down to if everyone has the Athletics excellency or not, which yes most exalted tend to end up having but it's crazy punishing if you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a way of mitigating scenery damage.<br /> Or Ox Bodies.<br /> Or use your Crippling Injury.<br /> Or have Solar Medicine patch you up.<br /> <br /> A starting Solar can have 22+ health levels. Losing ~8 right off the bat isn't a death sentence. With Stamina 3 and two Ox Bodies, a Solar is still in their -2s. It is entirely within the realm of possibility that a Medium range fall can leave a starting Solar in their -0s.<br /> <br /> Then the ST decides whether they Decisive kill the PCs or use Gambits to take them alive (or just Wither them some more).<br /> <br /> I get that if you're playing Exalted as intended, with Tomb of Dreams style characters, then sure this is pretty harsh. But against reasonable optimized PCs... I don't see it.<br /> <br /> But your input is noted. This is just my idea, I'm not even the ST here.<br /> <br /> How would you run the encounter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-18-2020, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T03:09:15-07:00","id":1403360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403357#post1403357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Digging a fifty foot pit doesn't strike me as beyond the Princes of the Earth, whether there's an opposing battlegroup or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's short range I'd say though, ranges are more than a little abstract but Medium being about as far as you can throw a javelin without magic it's quite the hole, and the fall damage table is generally be considered to be pretty harsh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403357#post1403357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you run the encounter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming no one is sitting on Surprise Anticipation Method + Keen Hearing and Touch (in which case I'd let them roll to hear the sappers in time to get out), I'd make them roll Per+Awareness-4 at difficulty 3 to wake up as the floor starts giving out in time to react. If they fail they take short range fall damage and are prone, on success they are on their feet and roll Dex+Athletics at difficulty 5 to avoid fall damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T20:06:37-07:00","id":1403471,"title":"","content":"Session is tomorrow, so my/the villain's current plan is a variant of JohnDoe's devilry. The Air aspect issue a challenge, a three on three battle for the fate of the island, with the promise of executing lots of innocent bystanders if the PCs delay or try anything funny. He'll meet them in the town's execution square where the campaign began, where criminals/anyone who looks at him funny are locked in a pot and drowned by the incoming tide.<br /> <br /> He'll be standing at the head of the square, along with the Earth aspect and a couple guards dressed as Immaculate Monks. As soon as the players appear, the Earth aspect will collapse the entire square, dropping the players through a short fall (5 levels of blunt damage, - 1/success on a Dex-Athletics roll) and into bondfires, with the golem battle group surrounding them. Meanwhile, the Air aspect will make ranged attacks from the edge of the pit, the Immaculate MONK battle group will rain poisoned arrows (using poison arrow frog venom), and the Earth aspect will throw boulders at anyone trying to climb out.<br /> <br /> And if the fight goes on too long, the tide will start coming in... <br /> <br /> All of this will be set up before the challenge is issued, so the players will have a chance to figure it out and turn the tables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 07-18-2020, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T23:46:40-07:00","id":1403491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403471#post1403471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this will be set up before the challenge is issued, so the players will have a chance to figure it out and turn the tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds neat. Let us know how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T03:26:39-07:00","id":1403506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403245#post1403245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>: They're not particularly attached to her-- about two sessions ago they tore through her guards and she went &quot;I surrender, I never liked those guys anyway!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> What matters is that you have a weakness to leverage that can affect positioning and action economy.<br /> A dead NPC can only be avenged, while one being agressively targeted by antagonists or bleeding out on the ground creates a choice and an opertunity to show what kind of a person your character is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T19:29:28-07:00","id":1403610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403491#post1403491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds neat. Let us know how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it didn't work out <i>quite </i>like how I expected (surprise).<br /> <br /> Last session, the party had kidnapped a noble and offered to ransom her for her weight in silver. The Dragonblooded baddie decided to try and turn the tables, disguising himself and his elites as common soldiers and bringing them all to the exchange (with the golems as the &quot;only significant escort&quot;). The players got warned by a spy they'd placed in his household, and skipped the meeting in favor of raiding their foes' barracks and defeating all the normal soldiers there.<br /> <br /> This session, then, they rushed back to try and catch the Dragonblooded on his way back, maybe manage some divide-and-conquer. The Air aspect had given up on his disguise at this point, but I think they forgot about the monks and Earth aspect, because they promptly started a fight-- despite the fact that the Eclipse in particular was low on motes. One brutal point-blank-range slog and two collapsed buildings later, the monks and both Dragonblooded were dead, the golems frozen without further orders, and the Eclipse and Dawn both sitting at 6 health levels of damage.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, maybe they weren't <i>quite </i>as well built for combat as I thought, but it was a pretty epic boss battle. The Eclipse freaked the hell out when the Air aspect started throwing lightning at her, which was delightful. (She then caught a bolt on her daiklave and redirected it straight up into the sky.)<br /> <br /> Many thanks to you guys for your help. I might not have been able to use JohnDoe's plan, but the discussion here made me a lot more confident about what three Solars can handle-- I definitely used charms and tactics a lot more ruthlessly than I might have otherwise, and the session was all the better for it.<br /> <br /> (edit: Also highly successful, for whatever it's worth: the players-roll-all-the-dice houserules I was talking about a little bit ago. I've been using them throughout the campaign, but they really proved their worth tonight. Four completely different enemies on the battlefield, and I had no more trouble than I would have running the encounter in, say, 5e D&amp;D. And my goodness do the turns flow more smoothly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 07-19-2020, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T03:48:07-07:00","id":1403638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403170-so-i-have-no-idea-how-to-judge-encounter-difficulty?p=1403610#post1403610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(edit: Also highly successful, for whatever it's worth: the players-roll-all-the-dice houserules I was talking about a little bit ago. I've been using them throughout the campaign, but they really proved their worth tonight. Four completely different enemies on the battlefield, and I had no more trouble than I would have running the encounter in, say, 5e D&amp;D. And my goodness do the turns flow more smoothly)</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst I was initially sceptical, I've been looking at Broken Worlds (the Kill Six Billion Demons RPG) and... it does look easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}